---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import BacklogChart from "../components/BacklogChart.astro";
import StatTiles from "../components/StatTiles.astro";
import { LAUNCHED } from "../lib/launch";
import { homeFigures, complianceDetail, humanDuration, inMonths, fmt, formatDate, formatDateShort } from "../lib/data";

const f = homeFigures();
const comp = complianceDetail();
// The register's currency is the President's report, not the history series.
const asAt = formatDate(f.schedule.asAt);
const pct = (comp.rate * 100).toFixed(1);
// The strongest cell in the by-government table is the best one, not the worst:
// if even the most favourable reading of the most favourable government is in
// single figures, there is no partisan story to tell.
const heroStats = [
  { label: "Waiting over a year", value: fmt(f.overOneYear) },
  { label: "Waiting over five years", value: fmt(f.overFiveYears) },
  { label: "Median wait so far", value: `${fmt(f.medianWait)} days` },
  { label: "Responses that met the deadline", value: `${pct}%` },
];
const bestGov = Math.max(...comp.governments.flatMap((g) => [g.byResponse.rate, g.byReport.rate]));
---

<Base
  title="Reports Parliament is still waiting on"
  description="A running count of the committee reports the Australian Government has not responded to, how long each has waited, and how often the deadline is met."
>
  <section class="wrap hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Senate committee reports · as at {asAt}</p>
    <p class="figure">{fmt(f.outstanding)}</p>
    <h1 class="claim">reports are waiting for a government response.</h1>
    <p class="lede measure">
      The longest has waited <strong>{humanDuration(f.oldest.daysOutstanding)}</strong>{" "}
      — {fmt(f.oldest.daysOutstanding)} days since the {f.oldest.body} committee
      tabled{" "}<em>{f.oldest.title}</em> on {formatDate(f.oldest.owedSince)}.
    </p>
    <p class="gap measure">
      The Senate asks for a response within <strong>three months</strong>.
      The median answer takes <strong>{inMonths(comp.medianDays)}</strong>.
    </p>
    <p class="measure">
      For <strong>{fmt(f.beingConsidered)}</strong> of them the government has said only
      that its response is being considered. That is the President’s own record of it,
      not our reading.
    </p>
    <p class="measure">
      In the House of Representatives, where the government is asked for six months rather
      than three, <strong>{fmt(f.house.outstanding)}</strong> reports are waiting and
      {" "}{fmt(f.house.overdue)} of those are past the deadline.
      {f.house.beingConsidered === f.house.outstanding
        ? " For every one of them, the government says only that its response is being considered."
        : ` For ${fmt(f.house.beingConsidered)} of them, the government says only that its response is being considered.`}
      {" "}<a href="/house/">The House register →</a>
    </p>

    <StatTiles stats={heroStats} />
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <BacklogChart points={f.history} peak={f.peak} />
  </section>

  <section class="wrap two-up">
    <div class="measure">
      <h2>The deadline is not a deadline</h2>
      <p>
        Of {fmt(comp.assessable)} responses tabled between {comp.firstYear} and
        {" "}{comp.lastYear}, {fmt(comp.onTime)} arrived inside the required three
        months — {pct} per cent. The median took {fmt(comp.medianDays)} days.
        More than half took longer than a year.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is not a story about one government. Attribute every late response to
        whoever tabled it, or to whoever was in office when the report was tabled: the
        two readings disagree about which government performs worst, and on neither
        reading does any of the four reach one response in ten inside the deadline.
        {" "}<a href="/senate/#compliance">Both readings, side by side →</a>
      </p>
      {LAUNCHED && (
        <p>
          And a response arriving is not the same as a report being answered:
          {" "}<a href="/senate/responses/">how the government answered →</a>
        </p>
      )}
    </div>
    <div class="measure">
      <h2>What this site is</h2>
      <p>
        When a parliamentary committee reports, the government is expected to say what it
        will do about the recommendations. Often it does not, or does so years later.
        There is no single public record of which reports are still waiting.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is that record. It is built from the Parliament’s own registers and the
        Tabled Documents database; each register follows its presiding officer — the
        President of the Senate and the Speaker of the House both report on the status of
        government responses, at roughly six-monthly intervals — and publishes what he
        records. Every page shows the date of the data behind it. The whole dataset is{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/toohardbasket-lab/toohardbasket">public</a>.
        Nothing here is an opinion about any recommendation — only whether an answer
        was given, and when.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap longest">
    <h2>Longest outstanding</h2>
    <table class="register">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col" class="num">Waiting</th>
          <th scope="col">Report</th>
          <th scope="col">Committee</th>
          <th scope="col" class="num">Tabled</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {f.ledger.slice(0, 10).map((r) => (
          <tr>
            <td class="num">{fmt(r.daysOutstanding)} days</td>
            <td>{r.title}</td>
            <td class="cmte">{r.body}</td>
            <td class="num">{formatDateShort(r.owedSince)}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="more"><a href="/senate/">All {fmt(f.outstanding)} reports in the Senate register →</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  /* Hero figure: one per view, >=48px, same sans, proportional figures. */
  .figure {
    font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 2rem + 8vw, 6.5rem);
    line-height: 0.95; font-weight: 650; letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .claim {
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 1rem + 1vw, 1.6rem); font-weight: 500;
    max-width: 22ch; margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
  }
  .hero .lede em { font-style: normal; color: var(--ink); }
  .gap {
    font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 0.95rem + 0.5vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.45; margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 0.9rem; border-left: 2px solid var(--series-1);
  }


  .two-up {
    display: grid; gap: 2rem 3rem; margin-block: 1rem 3rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(20rem, 1fr));
  }

  .longest h2 { margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
  .longest .cmte { color: var(--ink-secondary); font-size: 0.8125rem; }
  .longest td { padding-right: 1rem; }
  .more { font-size: 0.875rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
</style>
